arguments.prompt:
You are working on a Blazor Web App (Interactive Auto, Global, with Individual auth) at:
- Server project: /tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/
- Client project: /tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/

The app tracks shipments for a logistics company. Requirements:
- Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
- Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
- Users authenticate with individual accounts (already scaffolded via Identity)
- Interactive Auto global mode (already configured)

## CRITICAL Auto Mode Rules
- ALL interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Interactive components CANNOT access DbContext directly — use HTTP APIs
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient in `.Client` and with EF Core on server
- Register matching services in BOTH Program.cs files
- Server-only things (EF, Identity, API endpoints) stay in server project

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Models (in `.Client` project since both projects can reference it)

Create `/tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentStatus.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

Create `/tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string RecipientEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string? CustomerUserId { get; set; }
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in `.Client` project)

Create `/tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment);
    Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 3. Client-side HttpClient implementation (in `.Client` project)

Create `/tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync()
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments/my") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }
}
