The app tracks shipments for a logistics company. Requirements:
- Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
- Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
- Users authenticate with individual accounts (already scaffolded via Identity)
- Interactive Auto global mode (already configured)

## CRITICAL Auto Mode Rules
- ALL interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Interactive components CANNOT access DbContext directly — use HTTP APIs
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient in `.Client` and with EF Core on server
- Register matching services in BOTH Program.cs files
- Server-only things (EF, Identity, API endpoints) stay in server project

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Models (in `.Client` project since both projects can reference it)

Create `/tmp/sv-c4efb99b830f4b7c83721cdb69f34c6c/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentStatus.cs`:
